      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KINGS PARK (6) earns top billing after running third at Ascot in a CL1 when beaten a length despite starting at big odds. On the quick turnaround here, but the step to 1200m is a big tick and the wide draw is no issue. Looks ready to raise the bar again and that'll see him hard to hold out. UNIMANDO (2) is the clear danger, arriving off successive wins at Northam and this track, most recently beating Secret Planet in a CL1. Drawn better now and he'll give them something to chase once again. DIAMOND DANCER (1) has the exposed toughness, having gone under by a nose at Northam last start. The claim of Tsang helps and she's sure to be thereabouts if she can run to recent form. QUOKKA ROCKA (4) was disappointing as a well-backed runner first-up. He's better than that though and Whiting replacing the apprentice hoop is a good push. JOLSON AL (7) can feature third-up into the campaign.",
